Package: researchpaths
Title: Resolve Data Paths on Removable Volumes Without Guessing
Version: 0.1.0
Authors@R: person("Tyler", "Muffly", email = "tyler.muffly@dhha.org", role = c("aut", "cre"))
Description: Removable volumes mount under whatever name the operating system
    decides; macOS in particular remounts a drive as "Name 1" after an unclean
    unmount. Code that hardcodes a mount path then reads nothing -- and because
    DuckDB creates a database at a path that does not exist, the failure can be
    an empty warehouse and a pipeline that reports success having measured
    nothing. This package discovers volumes by glob, validates candidates before
    opening anything, never creates or modifies a candidate during discovery,
    and fails loudly on zero or ambiguous matches.
URL: https://mufflyt.github.io/researchpaths/, https://github.com/mufflyt/researchpaths
BugReports: https://github.com/mufflyt/researchpaths/issues
